Z||000000||btoth||05-22-2001||12:17 PM||||Well, I really got my car back last week, but then found out that my T.V. cable was broken so I ordered one from the Fiero Store and got it fixed and now it's better than ever!  Nice new 2.8 (with performance cam and other goodies - supposedly!) and it shifts perfectly, too!  Woohoo!<P>Now I just have to trace down this tiny electrical problem (volts were dropping yesterday) when the weather clears up enough.<P>This week I'm going to <I>finally</I> install my new GT quarter windows that I got for Christmas and fix up my interior... and maybe get that darned Flowmaster installed.  Hopefully then next summer I can actually get it painted and have it look decent on the outside.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||10
Z||000001||Raydar||05-22-2001||12:23 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by btoth:<BR><B>Now I just have to trace down this tiny electrical problem (volts were dropping yesterday) when the weather clears up enough.<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><BR>Is it raining? Sometimes when my belt gets wet it slips. Makes the voltmeter drop to 10-11 or so. Usually happens when I first start the car, after it's been raining. After a few seconds, the belt gets traction and the volts jump.<P>Congrats on getting it running.<BR><P>------------------<BR>Raydar - aka Steve<P>88 black Formula<BR>88 Duke coupe <BR>88 "wadded up" Formula (parts car)||||reg||1
